<%# The one place a verdict gets a colour, so the ledger and the detail page can
    never disagree about what amber means.

    Coloured by what the word DOES, matched loosely, because the vocabulary
    belongs to the gates and not to this app: `hold` is the gate stopping work,
    `auto-*` is it letting work through unattended, `authorized-*` is a human
    having said yes. A verdict none of those match is still rendered — grey, and
    legible — rather than dropped, which is what happens the first time a gate
    invents a word. %>
<% word = decision.to_s.strip %>
<% tone = if word.blank?                      then "bg-gray-100 text-gray-500"
          elsif word.match?(/hold/i)          then "bg-amber-100 text-amber-800"
          elsif word.match?(/\Aauto-?/i)      then "bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800"
          elsif word.match?(/authoriz|merge|proceed/i) then "bg-sky-100 text-sky-800"
          else "bg-gray-100 text-gray-700"
          end %>
<span class="inline-flex items-center px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-[11px] font-semibold whitespace-nowrap <%= tone %>"><%= word.presence || "—" %></span>
